We need produce JSON only with declaration, implementation, supporting_objects. Need design CODESYS 3.5 ST FB_Task. Need exact interface names/types from interface. Inputs/outputs. Need define DUT for phase enum maybe supporting object. Architectural plan gives phase states IDLE, FILL_A, FILL_B, FILL_C, MIX, DRAIN. Could define enum Phase. Need declare VAR sections.

Need implement behavior per assumptions. Need careful with mode change first invocation. Need edge memories. Need emergency stop clears latches and phase IDLE. ProcessMode latched at autoStart. DRAIN hold valve D until estop, mode switch manual, or fresh autoStart. AutoStart accepted IDLE or DRAIN to start fresh batch. One phase transition per invocation. Mode change after first invocation clears sequence/latches and suppresses commands, edge memories update. First invocation establishes selected mode and executes normally.

Need output assignments unified. Need think scan order.

We need compile offline. Use enum E_Phase maybe. In declaration VAR_INPUT, VAR_OUTPUT, VAR (private). Need initial values. In CODESYS, enumerated type default first value. Define E_Phase: (IDLE, FILL_A, FILL_B, FILL_C, MIX, DRAIN). initial phase E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE? In VAR declaration can set phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE; likely valid. Could set := IDLE maybe. Use E_Phase.IDLE.

Need maintain initialized BOOL, prevOpeMode BOOL, modeChange BOOL. Edge prev variables.

Need use rising expressions: edgeA := valveAStart AND NOT prevValveAStart; etc. Need compute at start. Then update prev variables at end? But if estop=FALSE, edge memories still update. Need update prev after computing edges regardless. We can compute edges and immediately update prev variables, or at end. If at end, okay. Need modeChange = initialized AND (opeMode <> prevOpeMode). Then update prevOpeMode and initialized. If first invocation, modeChange false. Need ensure prevOpeMode gets set. Could compute modeChange based on initialized and prevOpeMode, then set prevOpeMode := opeMode; initialized := TRUE.

Need emergency stop priority: if NOT estop then clear latches, phase IDLE? Assumption: Emergency stop resets all manual latches and automatic state. A fresh autoStart edge required to restart. Also "Emergency stop resets all manual latches and automatic state. A fresh autoStart edge is required to restart." It says emergency stop resets sequence to IDLE. Need on estop FALSE, phase IDLE, latches false, processModeLatched false? likely reset. But if estop FALSE and autoStart held? Edge memory updates so no rising after recovery. On estop scan edge memories update, prevAutoStart := autoStart. On recovery next scan, if held, no rising. If new press after recovery, rising. Good.

Need mode change after first invocation: clears sequence/latches, suppresses commands for that invocation; edge memories still update. That means if modeChange TRUE, set all latches false, phase IDLE, processModeLatched false? Clear old latches and sequence. Suppress outputs. But should we clear processModeLatched? "clears sequence/latches". ProcessModeLatched is batch latch; likely clear on reset. On modeChange reset, clear. If opeMode changes to AUTO on a scan, modeChange true, outputs off, phase IDLE; next scan if autoStart edge was ignored? Edge memory updated, so need fresh autoStart after mode change. Assumption says changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence. Mode-change suppression. Need not accept autoStart on modeChange scan. Good.

Need first invocation establishes selected mode and executes normally. If first invocation opeMode true and autoStart rising? Since prevAutoStart initial false, if autoStart true then rising true. Should accept autoStart in IDLE and start FILL_A on first invocation. initialized false => modeChange false. So yes.

Need automatic logic. Use CASE phase. Must evaluate exactly one transition per invocation using pre-scan phase. Need processModeLatched latched at batch start from processMode. For two-material: at FILL_B when level >=80 and processModeLatched FALSE -> MIX. For three: if TRUE -> FILL_C. Then FILL_C when >=100 -> MIX. MIX when mixMotorComplete -> DRAIN. DRAIN: if rising autoStart -> FILL_A and latch processMode; else hold D. IDLE: if rising autoStart -> FILL_A and latch processMode.

Need at autoStart start, latch processMode := processMode input. Also on DRAIN restart. Need ensure "processMode stays latched for active batch". If processMode input changes mid batch, latched used. Good.

Need output commands from phase and manual latches. Need "Automatic phases drive only one actuator; independent manual toggles may coexist." Wait safety_priority says "Automatic phases drive only one actuator; independent manual toggles may coexist." But P8 says G((safe & opeMode -> oneActuator) ...). In automatic mode at most one actuator. Manual toggles only in manual. "independent manual toggles may coexist" perhaps means in manual multiple outputs can be on. Automatic one. So output if opeMode true use phase only. If manual use latches.

Need "Mode-change priority ... suppresses commands for that invocation; edge memories still update. The first invocation establishes selected mode and executes normally." So if modeChange true, outputs off. What about phase? Clear to IDLE and latches. But if opeMode changed to manual, on same scan outputs off. Next scan manual latches false and manual buttons can toggle only with rising edges captured? Edge memories updated on modeChange scan. If button pressed same scan as mode change, rising computed true but manual toggle suppressed. Next scan held button no rising, so cannot toggle until fresh press. Good.

Need "Changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence." On modeChange, clear. On estop, clear. Need maybe set phase IDLE. If estop false while prev phase not IDLE, set IDLE.

Need "In DRAIN, valveDRun remains TRUE until emergency stop, mode switch to manual, or fresh autoStart edge starting new batch." If mode switch to AUTO? Mode change to auto also clears sequence? Requirement says mode switch to manual specifically, but assumption mode change clears. If opeMode true -> false, modeChange clear. If opeMode false -> true from manual, modeChange clear IDLE. Good. In DRAIN, if no autoStart, hold D. If autoStart rising, start FILL_A. If mixMotorComplete maybe irrelevant. DRAIN never auto exits otherwise.

Need "autoStart rising accepted in IDLE or DRAIN to start a fresh batch from FILL_A." Good.

Need threshold >=50, >=80, >=100. levelSensor INT. Use >=.

Need outputs assigned after state transitions. Need handle edge histories updating every scan. We can compute edges at top and update prev at top. That ensures edge memories update even if early return? We won't early return. Use BOOLs.

Potential issue with output variables in FB: We can read output variables? Not necessary.

Need include supporting object E_Phase DUT. Maybe no functions. Could define E_Phase as DUT kind DUT, declaration "(IDLE, FILL_A, FILL_B, FILL_C, MIX, DRAIN);" no implementation. In JSON supporting_objects each with name, kind, declaration, implementation. For DUT implementation maybe "". Need include return_type? Only functions need return_type. DUT no.

Need declaration string. CODESYS FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task followed by VAR sections. The instruction: "declaration is CODESYS FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task followed by all VAR sections; omit END_FUNCTION_BLOCK." So declaration should include "FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task" then VAR_INPUT ... END_VAR etc. It says omit END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. We'll include no END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. Implementation is ST body alone.

Need exact types: estop BOOL, opeMode BOOL, valveAStart BOOL, valveBStart BOOL, valveCStart BOOL, valveDStart BOOL, mixMotorStart BOOL, autoStart BOOL, processMode BOOL, levelSensor INT, mixMotorComplete BOOL. Outputs BOOL. Good.

Private variables:
phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE;
manualLatchA, B, C, D, Mix : BOOL := FALSE;
processModeLatched : BOOL := FALSE;
initialized : BOOL := FALSE;
prevOpeMode : BOOL := FALSE;
modeChange : BOOL := FALSE; (could be temp)
prevValveAStart, prevValveBStart, prevValveCStart, prevValveDStart, prevMixMotorStart, prevAutoStart : BOOL := FALSE;
Maybe edge temp variables in VAR: edgeA, edgeB, edgeC, edgeD, edgeMix, edgeAuto : BOOL; Could declare in VAR or local. In ST FB, we can use temp variables in VAR. Need maybe "modeChanged" vs modeChange. Use modeChange.

Need ensure initialized first invocation. We'll do:

// edge sampling
edgeA := valveAStart AND NOT prevValveAStart;
...
edgeAuto := autoStart AND NOT prevAutoStart;
prevValveAStart := valveAStart;
...
modeChange := initialized AND (opeMode <> prevOpeMode);
prevOpeMode := opeMode;
initialized := TRUE;

// priority
IF NOT estop THEN
    phase := E_Phase.IDLE;
    manualLatchA := FALSE; ...;
    processModeLatched := FALSE;
    valveARun := FALSE; ...; // perhaps assign here? But output assignment later will also. Need set a suppress flag.
    // Need no auto transition. Output assignment later if estop false all false.
ELSIF modeChange THEN
    phase := E_Phase.IDLE;
    manualLatch... false;
    processModeLatched := FALSE;
    // suppress outputs
ELSE
    IF opeMode THEN
        CASE phase OF
          IDLE:
             IF edgeAuto THEN
                 phase := FILL_A;
                 processModeLatched := processMode;
             END_IF;
          FILL_A:
             IF levelSensor >= 50 THEN phase := FILL_B; END_IF;
          FILL_B:
             IF levelSensor >= 80 THEN
                 IF processModeLatched THEN phase := FILL_C; ELSE phase := MIX; END_IF;
             END_IF;
          FILL_C:
             IF levelSensor >= 100 THEN phase := MIX; END_IF;
          MIX:
             IF mixMotorComplete THEN phase := DRAIN; END_IF;
          DRAIN:
             IF edgeAuto THEN
                 phase := FILL_A;
                 processModeLatched := processMode;
             END_IF;
        END_CASE;
    ELSE
        // manual mode
        IF edgeA THEN manualLatchA := NOT manualLatchA; END_IF;
        ...
    END_IF;
END_IF;

// Outputs
IF NOT estop THEN
   all false
ELSIF modeChange THEN
   all false
ELSIF opeMode THEN
   valveARun := (phase = FILL_A);
   valveBRun := (phase = FILL_B);
   valveCRun := (phase = FILL_C);
   valveDRun := (phase = DRAIN);
   mixMotorRun := (phase = MIX);
ELSE
   valveARun := manualLatchA;
   valveBRun := manualLatchB;
   valveCRun := manualLatchC;
   valveDRun := manualLatchD;
   mixMotorRun := manualLatchMix;
END_IF;

Need maybe when estop false, phase IDLE, processModeLatched false. But then recovery, if autoStart held no edge, phase IDLE. If opeMode true, no output. Good.

Need modeChange: If initialized false and opeMode whatever, modeChange false. After setting prevOpeMode, initialized true. If first scan opeMode true and autoStart rising, start. If first scan estop false, emergency resets; initialized true. Good.

Need subtle: On modeChange scan, we clear phase and latches and suppress outputs. But we also computed edges and updated prev. Good. If modeChange true and estop true, no auto/manual toggles. Next scan if opeMode true and autoStart held, edgeAuto false. Need fresh. Good.

Need "edge histories update during emergency stop so held buttons cannot restart outputs on recovery." We update prev at top always. Good.

Need "Changing operation mode clears old latches and sequence." We clear on modeChange. Good.

Need "Emergency stop resets ... A fresh autoStart edge required to restart." We clear. But do we clear processModeLatched on estop? yes. On recovery and autoStart rising, latch processMode.

Need "Mode-change priority: emergency stop first; then a change of mode after the first invocation clears sequence/latches and suppresses commands for that invocation; edge memories still update. The first invocation establishes the selected mode and executes normally." We handle.

Need "Automatic phases drive only one actuator; independent manual toggles may coexist." In auto, only one. In manual, multiple. Good.

Need "In DRAIN, valveDRun remains TRUE until emergency stop, mode switch to manual, or fresh autoStart rising edge starting a new batch." Our DRAIN if opeMode true and modeChange false, valveD true until edgeAuto. If opeMode switches manual, modeChange true that scan outputs off, phase IDLE. Good. If estop false, off. If fresh autoStart, phase FILL_A same scan, valveA true, D off. Good.

Need "ProcessMode latched at autoStart." We set when IDLE/DRAIN edgeAuto. But what if opeMode true, phase IDLE, autoStart rising, processMode true -> FILL_A. If processMode changes same scan? Input sample; latch current. Good.

Need "First invocation establishes selected mode and executes normally." If initialized false, modeChange false even if prevOpeMode default false and opeMode true. Good.

Potential issue: On first invocation, prevOpeMode default false; if opeMode false, modeChange false. If opeMode true, modeChange false. Good.

Need maybe use R_TRIG? Not necessary. Manual edge pattern is fine. No timers.

Need compile syntax. CODESYS ST uses "END_IF"; case labels "E_Phase.IDLE:"? In CASE statement, labels can be enumeration values: E_Phase.IDLE: valid. Or just IDLE? Better use E_Phase.IDLE. In CASE phase OF E_Phase.IDLE: ... E_Phase.FILL_A: ... END_CASE; CODESYS supports enum labels? Yes likely. Could use integer state to avoid enum issues. But phase in architecture is string. Define enum. To maximize compile, use enum with qualified labels in CASE. CODESYS supports CASE on enum and labels as enum constants. Use E_Phase.IDLE. Need define DUT E_Phase as "(IDLE, FILL_A, FILL_B, FILL_C, MIX, DRAIN);" In declaration, variable phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE; Is E_Phase.IDLE allowed in initialization? Usually yes. Could use := E_Phase.IDLE. Good.

Need include "FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task" line. Under declaration, maybe no semicolon after FUNCTION_BLOCK. Do:

FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
    estop : BOOL;
...
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
...
END_VAR
VAR
    phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE;
...
END_VAR

No END_FUNCTION_BLOCK.

Implementation ST body. Need ensure not use C-style. Use := and ;.

Need maybe "modeChange := initialized AND (opeMode <> prevOpeMode);" In ST, <> valid. "NOT estop" valid. "AND" "OR". Good.

Need decide whether to clear processModeLatched on modeChange. Yes.

Need consider output assignments when modeChange true and estop true. We set all false. But what about manual latches cleared. Good.

Need consider auto phase transition exactly one per invocation. CASE only one. But if IDLE and edgeAuto, phase := FILL_A. Then output assignment uses FILL_A. Good. If FILL_A level>=50, phase := FILL_B, output B. Good. If FILL_B level>=80 and processModeLatched false, phase := MIX, output mix. Good. If FILL_C level>=100, phase := MIX. Good. If MIX mixComplete, phase := DRAIN. Good. If DRAIN edgeAuto, phase := FILL_A. Good.

Need maybe autoStart rising in IDLE should not also be considered in same scan if phase changes? Since CASE only one. Good.

Need modeChange false but opeMode false: manual toggles. If estop true. Good.

Need "manual toggles may coexist" output assignment uses all latches. Good.

Potential issue: "Mode-change isolation: after first invocation, a change in opeMode clears manual latches and auto sequence, forces outputs OFF for that scan, while edge memories still update." Suppose modeChange true, we set phase IDLE and latches false. But if opeMode becomes false (manual) and valveAStart has rising edge same scan, we suppress manual toggle. Next scan if valveAStart held, edgeA false, so no toggle. Good.

Potential issue: "The first invocation establishes the selected mode and executes normally." If first invocation opeMode true, phase IDLE, autoStart false, no output. If first invocation opeMode false and valveAStart true, edgeA true, manualLatchA toggles true, output A true. Good. If first invocation opeMode true and autoStart true, start. Good.

Potential issue: "Emergency stop resets all manual latches and automatic state. A fresh autoStart edge is required to restart." On estop false scan, we clear phase and processModeLatched. But we update prevAutoStart at top. If autoStart was TRUE before estop and remains TRUE, edgeAuto false on recovery. If autoStart was FALSE before estop and becomes TRUE during estop, edgeAuto true on estop scan (because prev false) but auto logic suppressed due NOT estop. We update prevAutoStart true. On recovery held true, no edge. Good. If autoStart becomes true after recovery from false, edge true. Good.

Need maybe reset processModeLatched on modeChange even if opeMode true? yes.

Need maybe "manualLatch" variables reset on estop/modeChange. Good.

Need maybe output variables initial values. FB output default false. But initial_conditions says false. We don't need explicitly initialize outputs in VAR_OUTPUT? Could set := FALSE? In CODESYS, VAR_OUTPUT may accept initial values? Usually yes? To avoid syntax issues, leave default false. But initial observation before first scan? In CODESYS, FB outputs default false if not assigned. Good. But maybe tests reset instance, outputs are false. Good.

Need maybe "phase" in initial_conditions is string but internal. We define E_Phase. Good.

Need include supporting object E_Phase. Possibly no other supporting objects. Could define a function? Not needed.

Need output JSON object with keys "declaration", "implementation", "supporting_objects". Supporting_objects list with one object. Each object name, kind, declaration, implementation. For DUT, implementation maybe "". Should we include return_type? Not for DUT. The prompt: "functions need return_type." We have no functions. Good.

Need ensure JSON valid, escape newlines as \n. Use double quotes. Need no Markdown.

Let's craft declaration string:

"FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task\nVAR_INPUT\n    estop : BOOL;\n    opeMode : BOOL;\n    valveAStart : BOOL;\n    valveBStart : BOOL;\n    valveCStart : BOOL;\n    valveDStart : BOOL;\n    mixMotorStart : BOOL;\n    autoStart : BOOL;\n    processMode : BOOL;\n    levelSensor : INT;\n    mixMotorComplete : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n    valveARun : BOOL;\n    valveBRun : BOOL;\n    valveCRun : BOOL;\n    valveDRun : BOOL;\n    mixMotorRun : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n    phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE;\n    manualLatchA : BOOL := FALSE;\n    manualLatchB : BOOL := FALSE;\n    manualLatchC : BOOL := FALSE;\n    manualLatchD : BOOL := FALSE;\n    manualLatchMix : BOOL := FALSE;\n    processModeLatched : BOOL := FALSE;\n    initialized : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevOpeMode : BOOL := FALSE;\n    modeChange : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevValveAStart : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevValveBStart : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevValveCStart : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevValveDStart : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevMixMotorStart : BOOL := FALSE;\n    prevAutoStart : BOOL := FALSE;\n    edgeA : BOOL := FALSE;\n    edgeB : BOOL := FALSE;\n    edgeC : BOOL := FALSE;\n    edgeD : BOOL := FALSE;\n    edgeMix : BOOL := FALSE;\n    edgeAuto : BOOL := FALSE;\nEND_VAR"

Implementation string:

"// Edge sampling\nedgeA := valveAStart AND NOT prevValveAStart;\nedgeB := valveBStart AND NOT prevValveBStart;\nedgeC := valveCStart AND NOT prevValveCStart;\nedgeD := valveDStart AND NOT prevValveDStart;\nedgeMix := mixMotorStart AND NOT prevMixMotorStart;\nedgeAuto := autoStart AND NOT prevAutoStart;\n\nprevValveAStart := valveAStart;\nprevValveBStart := valveBStart;\nprevValveCStart := valveCStart;\nprevValveDStart := valveDStart;\nprevMixMotorStart := mixMotorStart;\nprevAutoStart := autoStart;\n\nmodeChange := initialized AND (opeMode <> prevOpeMode);\nprevOpeMode := opeMode;\ninitialized := TRUE;\n\n// Priority 1: emergency stop\nIF NOT estop THEN\n    phase := E_Phase.IDLE;\n    manualLatchA := FALSE;\n    manualLatchB := FALSE;\n    manualLatchC := FALSE;\n    manualLatchD := FALSE;\n    manualLatchMix := FALSE;\n    processModeLatched := FALSE;\n\n// Priority 2: mode-change isolation\nELSIF modeChange THEN\n    phase := E_Phase.IDLE;\n    manualLatchA := FALSE;\n    manualLatchB := FALSE;\n    manualLatchC := FALSE;\n    manualLatchD := FALSE;\n    manualLatchMix := FALSE;\n    processModeLatched := FALSE;\n\n// Priority 3/4: normal operation\nELSE\n    IF opeMode THEN\n        CASE phase OF\n            E_Phase.IDLE:\n                IF edgeAuto THEN\n                    phase := E_Phase.FILL_A;\n                    processModeLatched := processMode;\n                END_IF;\n\n            E_Phase.FILL_A:\n                IF levelSensor >= 50 THEN\n                    phase := E_Phase.FILL_B;\n                END_IF;\n\n            E_Phase.FILL_B:\n                IF levelSensor >= 80 THEN\n                    IF processModeLatched THEN\n                        phase := E_Phase.FILL_C;\n                    ELSE\n                        phase := E_Phase.MIX;\n                    END_IF;\n                END_IF;\n\n            E_Phase.FILL_C:\n                IF levelSensor >= 100 THEN\n                    phase := E_Phase.MIX;\n                END_IF;\n\n            E_Phase.MIX:\n                IF mixMotorComplete THEN\n                    phase := E_Phase.DRAIN;\n                END_IF;\n\n            E_Phase.DRAIN:\n                IF edgeAuto THEN\n                    phase := E_Phase.FILL_A;\n                    processModeLatched := processMode;\n                END_IF;\n\n            ELSE\n                phase := E_Phase.IDLE;\n        END_CASE;\n    ELSE\n        IF edgeA THEN\n            manualLatchA := NOT manualLatchA;\n        END_IF;\n        IF edgeB THEN\n            manualLatchB := NOT manualLatchB;\n        END_IF;\n        IF edgeC THEN\n            manualLatchC := NOT manualLatchC;\n        END_IF;\n        IF edgeD THEN\n            manualLatchD := NOT manualLatchD;\n        END_IF;\n        IF edgeMix THEN\n            manualLatchMix := NOT manualLatchMix;\n        END_IF;\n    END_IF;\nEND_IF;\n\n// Unified output assignments\nIF NOT estop THEN\n    valveARun := FALSE;\n    valveBRun := FALSE;\n    valveCRun := FALSE;\n    valveDRun := FALSE;\n    mixMotorRun := FALSE;\nELSIF modeChange THEN\n    valveARun := FALSE;\n    valveBRun := FALSE;\n    valveCRun := FALSE;\n    valveDRun := FALSE;\n    mixMotorRun := FALSE;\nELSIF opeMode THEN\n    valveARun := (phase = E_Phase.FILL_A);\n    valveBRun := (phase = E_Phase.FILL_B);\n    valveCRun := (phase = E_Phase.FILL_C);\n    valveDRun := (phase = E_Phase.DRAIN);\n    mixMotorRun := (phase = E_Phase.MIX);\nELSE\n    valveARun := manualLatchA;\n    valveBRun := manualLatchB;\n    valveCRun := manualLatchC;\n    valveDRun := manualLatchD;\n    mixMotorRun := manualLatchMix;\nEND_IF;"

Need verify "NOT estop" when estop is BOOL. Good.

Potential issue: In CODESYS, CASE label "E_Phase.IDLE:" is okay? I think yes. But some compilers require "E_Phase.IDLE:" with colon. Good.

Potential issue: Using "ELSE" in CASE with enum. Good.

Potential issue: The FB_Task declaration references E_Phase DUT. Supporting object provides it. Good.

Potential issue: In CODESYS, VAR_OUTPUT cannot have initial value? We don't. Good.

Potential issue: In declaration, "phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE;" In CODESYS, for enum variable initialization, syntax might be "phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE;" yes. If not, could use "phase : E_Phase := IDLE;" but qualified is okay. Need compile. I've seen CODESYS use "eState : E_State := E_State.Idle;" yes.

Potential issue: "modeChange := initialized AND (opeMode <> prevOpeMode);" On first scan initialized false, prevOpeMode default false. Then prevOpeMode := opeMode. Good. If first scan opeMode true, modeChange false. Good.

Potential issue: We set initialized TRUE at start. Then later use modeChange. Good.

Potential issue: On modeChange scan, we clear processModeLatched. Suppose opeMode changes from manual to auto and autoStart rising same scan. modeChange true; we clear and suppress. EdgeAuto updated. Next scan autoStart held -> no edge. Must release and press. Assumption says fresh autoStart edge required? It says mode change clears old latches and sequence; new commands accepted on subsequent invocations subject to edge rules. So yes.

Potential issue: "autoStart is a rising edge accepted in IDLE or DRAIN to start a fresh batch from FILL_A; processMode stays latched for the active batch (phases 1..5)." Our DRAIN with edgeAuto restarts; IDLE with edgeAuto starts. Good.

Potential issue: "Emergency stop resets all manual latches and automatic state. A fresh autoStart edge is required to restart." On estop false, we clear processModeLatched. On recovery, if phase IDLE and autoStart rising, starts. Good.

Potential issue: "In DRAIN, valveDRun remains TRUE until emergency stop, mode switch to manual, or a fresh autoStart rising edge starting a new batch." What if modeChange due to opeMode true->false? modeChange true outputs off, phase IDLE. Good. What if modeChange due to opeMode false->true from manual? It also clears. Good.

Potential issue: Manual mode with opeMode false and estop true. We process manual toggles every scan. If level sensors etc irrelevant. Good.

Potential issue: "Emergency permissive dominates mode and buttons." Our estop false resets and outputs off, ignores toggles. Good.

Potential issue: "Edge memories update during emergency stop so held buttons cannot restart outputs on recovery." Our prev updated at top even estop false. Good.

Potential issue: "A transition affects the same observed scan." Our outputs after state update. Good.

Potential issue: "One logical phase transition occurs per invocation." Our CASE. Good.

Potential issue: "Automatic mode turns on at most one actuator at any scan" Our output from phase single. Good. But in auto mode, manual latches could be true from previous manual? We clear on modeChange to auto. But suppose modeChange false and opeMode true, manual latches might be true if somehow set? We only set manual latches in opeMode false. When switching from manual to auto, modeChange true clears. On first invocation if opeMode true, latches default false. So okay. Output ignores latches in auto. Good.

Potential issue: "Independent manual toggles may coexist." Our manual mode can have multiple latches true. Good.

Potential issue: "Mode switch to manual" in DRAIN: If opeMode true and DRAIN, then opeMode goes false. modeChange true, clear phase IDLE. Output off. Good.

Need maybe include "processModeLatched" clear on estop/modeChange. Good.

Need maybe include "manualLatch" cleared on estop/modeChange. Good.

Need maybe include "phase" initial E_Phase.IDLE. Good.

Need maybe include "modeChange" variable in VAR. Good.

Need maybe include "edgeA" etc in VAR. Good.

Need maybe include "E_Phase" DUT in supporting_objects. The DUT declaration should be:

"TYPE E_Phase :\n(\n    IDLE,\n    FILL_A,\n    FILL_B,\n    FILL_C,\n    MIX,\n    DRAIN\n);\nEND_TYPE"

Or simpler: "TYPE E_Phase : (IDLE, FILL_A, FILL_B, FILL_C, MIX, DRAIN); END_TYPE". CODESYS DUT syntax: 
TYPE E_Phase :
(
    IDLE,
    FILL_A,
    ...
);
END_TYPE
Yes. Need supporting object kind "DUT". Implementation "".

The prompt says supporting_objects is a list of helper DUT/POU objects, each with name, kind (DUT/FUNCTION/FUNCTION_BLOCK), declaration, implementation; functions need return_type. For DUT, no return_type. Good.

Need ensure JSON string newlines escaped. We can output pretty JSON with actual newlines inside strings? JSON strings cannot contain literal newlines. Need use \n. The final answer should be JSON object. We'll produce with escaped newlines. That's acceptable. Need no Markdown. Ensure valid JSON. Could use JSON object with strings containing \n. No trailing commas. 

Let's double-check implementation syntax. We use comments with //. In ST, comments okay. In JSON string, // no issue. We have semicolons. 

Potential issue: CODESYS does not allow variable declaration "phase : E_Phase := E_Phase.IDLE;" if E_Phase is a DUT defined after FB? In CODESYS, order doesn't matter. Good.

Potential issue: If supporting object E_Phase is defined, compile. Good.

Potential issue: The declaration includes "FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task" and no END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. The prompt says omit END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. Good. But CODESYS syntax normally requires END_FUNCTION_BLOCK. The task expects declaration only, so okay.

Potential issue: The implementation body includes all logic. Good.

Potential issue: Use "ELSIF" not "ELSE IF". Good.

Potential issue: In CASE statement, after "E_Phase.DRAIN:" we have IF edgeAuto THEN ... END_IF; Then "ELSE" for case. Good. Need "END_CASE;" after. Good.

Potential issue: In CASE, label "E_Phase.IDLE:" and then statements. Good.

Potential issue: We set processModeLatched := processMode on edgeAuto. If processMode false, latch false. Good.

Potential issue: "processMode stays latched for active batch (phases 1..5)." In our FILL_B uses latched. Good. In FILL_C->MIX no need. In DRAIN restart latches new. Good.

Potential issue: "When liquid level sensor reaches 80cm, close valve B. Based on processMode: If processMode=false, start mixing motor; ... If processMode=true, open valve C; when reaches 100, close C, start mixing." Our FILL_B with level>=80 and latched false -> MIX (mix motor). Latched true -> FILL_C (C). Good.

